    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0190" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v13/pg158"/>

                <head>105. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Turkey<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d105-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-08-24T18:02:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 24,
                                1957—6:02 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>569. We have been holding conversations with King Hussein concerning the types of
                    military items which we might assist Jordan to obtain through the $10 million we
                    have made available for this purpose. On August 19 in Amman King in conversation
                    with Mallory asked that we consider furnishing regiment (which would be 36) of
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">with</hi>] M47 tanks.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d105-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Ankara should inform King we agree furnish this number M47s.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d105-f3"/> We assume he will wish also obtain at least one year’s
                    spare parts for each tank as well as ammunition.</p>
                <pb facs="0191" n="159" xml:id="pg159"/>
                <p>Ankara may wish consider desirability Henderson’s conveying this information to
                    King.</p>
                <p>Amman should inform Rifai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d105-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d105-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 785.56/8–2457. Secret; Priority.
                    Drafted by Rockwell; cleared with OSD; and approved and signed by Dulles. Also
                    sent to Amman and repeated to Istanbul and to Paris for USCINCEUR and
                    DEFREPNAMA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d105-f2" n="2" xml:id="d105-f2-content">
                <p>Mallory reported the conversation in telegram 336 from Amman, August 21. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi> 785.56/8–2157)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d105-f3" n="3" xml:id="d105-f3-content">
                <p>King Hussein was in Turkey August 22–25.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
